    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Dylan Beavers** (68.02) and **Bryce Harper** (75.45) headline our offensive output. **Dylan Beavers** finds himself in a premier situation batting leadoff against Montero, benefiting from a +5% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup that pushes him into our elite start tier. **Bryce Harper** remains the anchor of the lineup despite facing a decent arm; his combination of an elite #3 spot in the order and a favorable 4.84 xERA matchup provides a reliable floor of 75.45. Additionally, **Luis Arraez** (66.61) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.76) offer strong volume potential, with both players catching favorable winds and SPs with xERAs above 4.25, ensuring they remain high-priority starts in a league where batting average and efficiency are paramount.\n\nThe toughest call for today\u2019s lineup involved **Braden Montgomery** (43.75), who narrowly missed the final cut. While he possesses some upside, he is neutralized by a difficult matchup against Fried\u2019s 3.97 xERA, making him a marginal play compared to the higher floor provided by the likes of **Daulton Varsho** (57.71) or **Taylor Ward** (55.95). We are also navigating a significant blow to our depth: **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is unavailable due to a confirmed rainout, removing our most consistent producer from contention. Conversely, while players like **Lawrence Butler** (44.29) occupy the lower end of our starting range, his presence is necessitated by the hunt for stolen bases and specific roster constraints, though he faces risk due to a negative platoon split against Tolle. \n\nWe are closely monitoring the status of **Yainer Diaz** and **Cal Raleigh**, both of whom are confirmed out of their respective lineups today and remain on our bench. The rest of the bench\u2014including **Matt Chapman**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **JJ Bleday**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Zack Gelof**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, **Will Smith**, and **Tyler Freeman**\u2014will remain in reserve to preserve our game cap allotment. Managers should be particularly wary of the matchup for **Masyn Winn** (54.75), who faces the dual threat of a sub-5.00 xERA arm and a high-SB-suppression pitcher, potentially limiting his base-stealing opportunities today.",
